# Synthetic Task Board

## The idea
A small shared ticket board for a demo.

## What the demo must show
List and close a ticket.

## Must work
- List tickets
- Close a ticket

## Explicitly out of scope
- Billing
- Offline sync

## Stack the team already knows
TypeScript; SQL
## Scope
Ticket list UI.
## What I own
src/TicketList.ts reads response.tickets from GET /api/tickets.
## What I need from other roles
Backend implements POST /api/tickets/:id/close.
## Decisions made
No optimistic updates. Reload the list after a successful close.
## Still unclear
Loading presentation is not agreed.
Synthetic evaluation fixture. No real accounts, network services, or credentials.
export async function loadTickets(fetcher) {
  const response = await fetcher("/api/tickets");
  const body = await response.json();
  return body.tickets;
}
export async function closeTicket(fetcher, id) {
  return fetcher("/api/tickets/" + id + "/close", { method: "POST" });
}
export const paths = { list: "/api/tickets", close: "/api/tickets/:id/close" };
export function listTickets() { return { tickets: [{ id: "t1", title: "Demo", closed: false }] }; }
export function closeTicket(id) { return { id, closed: true }; }
export function sessionPolicy() { return 'not yet agreed'; }
